wJû deú sulleitourgoiú, diaú thún spoudhún eijû
touúû ptwcouúû, prosfevrousi timwvmenoi.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0055"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>nq'. Diavkonoi eJptaú ojfeivlousin eiønai kataú toún kanovna,
kaÞén pavnu megavlh eiæh hJ povliû× peisqeivshé deú</FOREIGN> <NOTE N="*" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0055" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0055C"></COL> Non video quomodo constare possit phrasis cum hoc participio feminino. Forte legendum  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>peisqhvshé.</FOREIGN>   <ED>EDIT</ED> .</NOTE>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aæpoú thðû bivblou
twðn pravxewn.</FOREIGN></P></DIV2> <DIV2 COM="0055" SECOND="NO"><P COM="0055"><COL N="0054C"></COL> XLVI. Presbyter si uxorem duxerit, ordine suo
moveatur; si autem fornicatus fuerit, vel adulterium
commiserit, penitus extrudatur, et ad poenitentiam
redigatur.</P> <P COM="0054">XLVII. Mulier si duobus fratribus nupserit, abjiciatur
 <COL N="0054D"></COL> us ue ad mortem; verumtamen in morte, si
promiserit quod ubi convaluerit, solvet matrimonium,
propter humanitatem, poenitentiam habebit.
Sed si mortua fuerit mulier, in hujusmodi conjugio
existens, vel ejus maritus, difficilis erit poenitentia
remanenti.</P> <P COM="0054">XLVIII. De iis qui in plurimas nuptias incidunt,
tempus quidem definitum manifestum est: conversio
autem ac fides ipsorum tempus contrahit.</P> <P COM="0054">XLIX. Si quis mulierem concupiscens, proposuerit
cum ea concumbere, ejus autem desiderium ad opus
non venerit, videtur esse gratia servatus.</P> <P COM="0054">L. Catechumenus si in dominicum ingrediens, in
ordine catechumenorum steterit, is autem peccat:
si genu quidem flectens, audiat non amplius peccans:
sin autem etiam audiens peccet, expellatur</P> <P COM="0054"><COL N="0056A"></COL> LI. De ea quae uterum gerit, quod oporteat eam
baptizari quando voluerit. Nihil enim in hoc, ea quae
parit, nascenti communicat, quia proprium uniuscujusque
propositum in confessione ostendatur.</P> <P COM="0056">LII. Presbyter in digamorum nuptiis ne convivetur.
Cum enim poenitentiam requirat digamus, quis
erit presbyter qui illas nuptias isto convivio comprobet?</P> <P COM="0056">LIII. Si alicujus uxorem, cum esset laicus, adulteratam
fuisse evidenter fuerit comprobatum, talis ad
ministerium venire non potest. Sin autem etiam
post ordinationem adulterata fuerit, dimittere eam
convenit. Quod si cum illa convixerit, non potest sibi
commissum ministerium habere.</P> <P COM="0056">LIV. Si presbyter qui corporale peccatum admiserit,
 <COL N="0056B"></COL> promotus fuerit, et confessus fuerit, quod ante
ordinationem peccaverit: non offerat, manens in
aliis, propter aliud ejus vitae studium; reliqua enim
peccata dixerunt multi per manus impositionem
tolli. Quod si ipse non confiteatur, aperte autem
convinci non potuerit, potestatis suae judicio relinquatur.</P> <P COM="0056">LV. Similiter et diaconus, si in idem peccatum
inciderit, ministri ordinem habeat.</P> <P COM="0056">LVI. Presbyter ante triginta annos non ordinetur,
etiamsi valde dignus fuerit, sed hoc tempus observet.
Dominus enim Jesus Christus trigesimo anno
baptizatus est, et coepit docere</P> <P COM="0056">LVII. Si quis in morbo constitutus illuminatus fuerit,
ad honorem presbyterii promoveri non potest:
fides enim ejus non est ex proposito, sed ex necessitate:
 <COL N="0056C"></COL> nisi forte propter sequens ejus studium et fidem,
atque hominum raritatem.</P> <P COM="0056">LVIII. Regionarii presbyteri, in dominico civitatis
offerre non possunt, praesente episcopo, vel presbyteris
urbis, neque panem dare in oratione, neque calicem;
sin autem absint, et ad orationem solus vocatus
fuerit, dare poterit. Chorepiscopi autem, sunt
quidem ad exemplum septuaginta, ut autem comministri,
propter studium in pauperes, offerunt honorati.</P> <P COM="0056">LIX. Diaconi septem esse debent secundum canonem,
etiamsi sit magna civitas: ejus autem rei fidem
faciet liber Actorum  <CITN>(Act. VI)</CITN> .</P></DIV2></DIV1> <DIV1 COM="0056" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0056">CONCILII GANGRENSIS
CANONES XX (An. Chr. 325). <NOTE TYPE=chad ANCHORED=N COM="0055" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0055"></COL> The Latin and Greek versions of the following work are printed in parallel in Migne.</NOTE></HEAD> <COL N="0055"></COL> <DIV2 COM="0055" SECOND="NO"><P COM="0055"><COL N="0055D"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>x'. Eiæ tiû toún gavmon mevmfoito, kaiú thún kaqeuvdousan
metaú touð ajndroúû aujthðû, ouøsan pisthún kaiú eujsebhð kaiú
eujlabhð, bdeluvssoito hÞ mevmfoito, wJû aÞn mhú dunamevnhn
eijû basileivan eijselqeiðn, ajnavqema eæstw.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0055"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>xa'. Eiæ tiû ejsqivonta kreva, cwriúû aiåmatoû, kaiú eijdwloquvtou
kaiú pniktouð, met1 eujlabeivaû kaiú pivstewû, katakrivnei,
wJû aÞn diaú toú metalambavnein, ejlpivda mhú eæconta,
ajnavqema eæstw.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0055"><COL N="0057A"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>xb'. Eiæ tiû douðlon profavsei qeosebeiçaû didavskei katafroneiðn
despovtou, kaiú ajnacwreiðn thðû uJphresivaû, kaiú mhú
met1 eujnoivaû kaiú pavshû timhðû twðé eJautouð despovthðé ejxuphreteiðsqai, ajnavqema eæstw.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0057"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>xg'. Eiv tiû diakrivnoito paraú presbutevrou gegamhkovtoû,
wû mhú crhðnai leitourghvsantoû aujtouð prosforaðû metalambavnein,
ajnavqema eæstw.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0057"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>xd'. Eiæ tiû didavskei toún oiøkon touð Qeouð eujkatafrovnhton
eiønai, kaiú taúû ejn aujtwðé sunavxeiû, ajnavqema eæstw.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0057"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>xe'. Eiæ tiû paraú thún ejkklhsivan ijdivaé ejkklhsiavzei, kaiú
katafronwðn thðû ejkklhsivaû, taú thðû ejkklhsivaû ejqevloi pravttein
mhú sunovntoû touð presbutevrou kataú gnwvmhn touð
ejpiskovpou, ajnavqema eæstw.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0057"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>x¾' Eiæ tiû karpoforivaû ejkklhsiastikaúû ejqevlei lambavnein,
 <COL N="0057B"></COL> hÞ didovnai eæxw thðû ejkklhsivaû paraú gnwvmhn touð ejpiskovpou
hÞ touð ejgkeceirismevnou taú toiauðta, kaiú mhú metaú
gnwvmhû aujtouð ejqevlei pravttein, ajnavqema eæstw.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0057"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>xz'. Eiæ tiû didoið hÞ lambavnoi karpoforivan parektoúû touð
ejpiskovpou, hÞ touð ejpitetagmevnou eijû oijkonomivan eujpoiièaû,
kaiú oJ didouúû, kaiú oJ lambavnwn, ajnavqema eæstw.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0057"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>xh'. Eiæ tiû parqeneuvoi hÞ ejgkrateuvoito, wJû aÞn bdeluvttwn
twðn gavmwn [bdeluttovmenoû toún gavmon] ajnacwrhvsaû,
kaiú mhú diaú touð [di1 aujtoú toú] kaloún kaiú aågion thðû parqenivaû,
ajnavqema eæstw.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0057"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>xq'. Eiæ tiû twðn parqeneuovntwn diaú toún kuvrion, katepaivroito
twðn gegamhkovtwn, ajnavqema eæstw.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0057"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>o'. Eiæ tiû katafronoivh twðn ejk pivstewû ajgavpaû poiouvntwn,
 <COL N="0057C"></COL> kaiú diaú timhún touð kurivou sugkalouvntwn touúû ajdelfouúû,
kaiú mhú ejqevloi koinwneiðn taiðû klhvsesi, diaú toú ejxeutelivzein
toú ginovmenon, ajnavqema eæstw.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0057"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oa'. Eiæ tiû ajndrwðn diaú nomizomevnhn aæskhsin peribolaivwé
crhðtai [kevcrhtai], kaiú wJû aÞn ejk touvtou thún dikaiosuvnhn
eæcwn, katayhfivsoito twðn met1 eujlabeivaû touúû
bhvrouû forouvntwn, kaiú thðé aællhé koinhðé kaiú ejn sunhqeivaé
ouæshé ejsqhðti kecrhmevnwn, ajnavqema eæstw.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0057"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ob'. Eiæ tiû gunhú diaú nomizomevnhn aæskhsin metabavlloito
ajmfivasma, kaiú ajntiú touð eijwqovtoû gunaikeivou ajmfiavsmatoû,
ajndreiðon [ajndrwðon] ajnalavboi [ajnalambavnoi], ajnavqema
eæstw.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0057"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>og'. Eiæ tiû gunhú katalimpavnoi toún aændra, kaiú ajnacwreiðn
ejqevloi, bdhluttomevnh toún gavmon, ajnavqema eæstw.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0057"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>od'. Eiæ tiû katalimpavnei taú eJautouð tevkna, kaiú mhú
 <COL N="0057D"></COL> [mhdeú] teknotrofeið, kaiú toú oåson eJautwðé [ejf1 eJautwðé] provû
qeosevbeian thún proshvkousan ajnavgoi [aægei], ajllaú profavsei
thðû ajskhvsewû ajmeloivh, ajnavqema eæstw.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0057"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oe'. Eiæ tina tevkna gonevwn, mavlista pistwðn, ajnacwroivh
profavsei qeosebeivaû, kaiú mhú thún kaqhvkousan timhún toiðû
goneuðsin ajponevmoi, protimwmevnhû dhlonovti par1 aujtoiðû
thðû qeosebeivaû, ajnavqema eæstw.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0057"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>o¾'. Eiæ tiû gunaikwðn diaú nomizomevnhn aæskhsin [qeosebeivan]
ajpokeivroito taúû kovmaû, aÝû eædwken oJ Qeoúû eij û uJpovmnhsin
thðû uJpotaghðû, wJû ajnaluvousa [paraluvsasa] provstagma
thðû uJpotaghðû, ajnavqema eæstw.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0057"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oz'. Eiæ tiû diaú nomizomevnhn aæskhsin ejn thðé kuriakhðé nhsteuvoi,
ajnavqema eæstw.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0057"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oh'. Eiæ tiû twðn ajskoumevnwn, cwriúû swmatikhðû ajnavgkhû
 <COL N="0059A"></COL> uJperhfaneuvoito, kaiú taúû paradedomevnaû nhsteivaû
eijû toú koinoún, kaiú fulassomevnaû uJpoú thðû ejkklhsivaû
paraluvei, ajpokurouðntoû</FOREIGN>  [ <HI REND="ITALIC">Zon.</HI>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uJpoikourouðntoû] ejn aujtwðé
teleivou logismouð, ajnavqema eæstw.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0059"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oq'. Eiæ tiû aijtiwðéto [aijtiaðtai] uJperhfavnwé diaqevsei kecrhmevnoû,
kaiú bdelussomenoû taúû sunavxeiû twðn martuvrwn,
hÞ taúû ejn aujtoiðû ginomevnaû leitourgivaû, kaiú taúû mnhvmaû
aujtwðn, ajnavqema eæstw.</FOREIGN></P></DIV2> <DIV2 COM="0059" SECOND="NO"><P COM="0059"><COL N="0056D"></COL> LX.—1. Si quis nuptias accuset, et dormientem
cum viro suo, fidelem piamque ac religiosam, detestetur
ac vituperet, quasi non possit in regnum Dei
introire, anathema sit.</P> <P COM="0056">LXI.—2. Si quis carnem edentem, absque sanguine,
et idolis immolato et suffocato, cum pietate
et fide, condemnat, uti spem non habentem, propter
hujusmodi perceptionem, anathema sit.</P> <P COM="0056"><COL N="0058A"></COL> LXII.—3. Si quis servum, divini cultus praetextu,
dominum contemnere doceat, et ab ejus obsequio
discedere, nec ei bona fide et omni honore servire,
anathema sit.</P> <P COM="0058">LXIII.—4. Si quis discernit presbyterum conjugatum,
quasi non oporteat, eo ministrante, ejus
oblationi communicare, anathema sit.</P> <P COM="0058">LXIV.—5. Si quis docet domum Dei contemnendam
esse, et conventus qui in ea celebrantur, anathema
sit.</P> <P COM="0058">LXV.—6. Si quis extra ecclesiam privatim conciones
habet: et Ecclesiam contemnens, quae sunt
Ecclesiae vult agere, non astante presbytero cum
voluntate episcopi, anathema sit.</P> <P COM="0058">LXVI.—7. Si quis ecclesiasticas fructuum oblationes
 <COL N="0058B"></COL> extra ecclesiam accipere aut dare voluerit,
praeter consensum episcopi, vel ejus cui hujusmodi
officia commissa sunt, nec cum ejus voluerit agere
consilio, anathema sit.</P> <P COM="0058">LXVII.—8. Si quis dederit vel acceperit fructuum
oblationes, praeter episcopum, vel eum qui constitutus
est ad dispensationem beneficentiae: et qui dat,
et qui accipit, anathema sit.</P> <P COM="0058">LXVIII.—9. Si quis virginitatem custodiens aut
continentiae studens, velut abhorrens nuptias, secedat,
non ideo quia sancta sit virginitas, neque propter
ipsum virginitatis bonum, anathema sit.</P> <P COM="0058">LXIX.—10. Si quis virginitatem servans propter
Dominum, se supra conjugatos extollat, anathema sit.</P> <P COM="0058">LXX.—11. Si quis illos despicit, qui agapas ex
 <COL N="0058C"></COL> fide faciunt, et propter honorem Domini convocant
fratres, et noluerit hujusmodi vocationibus communicare,
parvipendens quod agitur, anathema sit.</P> <P COM="0058">LXXI.—12. Si quis vir, ob eam quae existimatur
pietatis exercitationem, utatur peribolaeo, hoc
est amictu pallii: et velut in hoc justitiam constituens,
condemnet eos qui cum pietate beris et alia
communi solitaque veste utuntur, anathema sit.</P> <P COM="0058">LXXII.—13. Si qua mulier, propter eam quae
existimatur pietatis exercitationem, vestem mutet,
et pro solita veste muliebri, virilem sumat, anathema
sit.</P> <P COM="0058">LXXIII.—14. Si qua mulier a marito suo divertat,
et secedere velit, nuptias abhorrens, anathema sit.</P> <P COM="0058">LXXIV.—15. Si quis filios suos deserat, et eos
 <COL N="0058D"></COL> non alat, et quantum in se est ad pietatem et debitum
Dei cultum non instituat: sed exercitationis
praetextu, negligit, anathema sit.</P> <P COM="0058">LXXV.—16. Si qui filii secedant a parentibus,
maxime fidelibus, divini cultus praetextu, debitumque
parentibus honorem non exhibeant, praeposito videlicet
apud ipsos divino cultu, anathema sit.</P> <P COM="0058">LXXVI.—17. Si qua mulier, propter eam quae
existimatur pietatis exercitationem, comam tondeat,
quam Deus ei dedit in memoriam subjectionis, ut
quae subjectionis praeceptum dissolvat, anathema sit.</P> <P COM="0058">LXXVII.—18. Si quis, ob eam quae existimatur
pietatis exercitationem, Dominico die jejunat, anathema
sit.</P> <P COM="0058">LXXVIII.—19. Si quis eorum, qui pietatis exercitationi
 <COL N="0060A"></COL> student, absque necessitate corporis, insolescat,
et tradita in commune jejunia et ab Ecclesia
observata dissolvat, nimirum perfecta, quae in eo est,
ratiocinatione illa improbante, anathema sit.</P> <P COM="0060">LXXIX.—20. Si quis superbo affectu utens, et
abhorrens conventus martyrum, et sacra quae in eis
celebrantur, et eorum memorias, anathema sit.</P></DIV2></DIV1> <DIV1 COM="0060" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0060">CONCILII ANTIOCHENI
CANONES XXV (An. Chr. 341). <NOTE TYPE=chad ANCHORED=N COM="0059" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0059"></COL> The Latin and Greek versions of the following work are printed in parallel in Migne.</NOTE></HEAD> <COL N="0059"></COL> <DIV2 COM="0059" SECOND="NO"><P COM="0059"><COL N="0059A"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>p'. Pavntaû touúû tolmwðntaû paraluvein [parabaivnein] toún
 <COL N="0059B"></COL> oåron thðû aJgivaû kaiú megavlhû sunovdou thðû ejn Nikaivaé sugkrothqeivshû
ejpiú parousivaé thðû eujsebeivaû touð qeofilestavtou
basilevwû Kwnstantivnou, periú thðû aJgivaû eJorthðû touð
swthriwvdouû pavsca, ajkoinwnhvtouû. kaiú ajpoblhvtouû eiønai
thðû ejkklhsivaû, eij ejpimevnoien filoneikovteron ejnistavmenoi
proúû taú kalwðû dedogmevna. Kaiú tauðta eijrhvsqw periú twðn
laiçkwðn. Eij dev tiû twðn proestwvtwn thðû ejkklhsivaû, ejpivskopoû
hÞ presbuvteroû hÞ diavkonoû, metaú toún oåron touðton
tolmhvseien ejpiú diastrofhðé twðn lawðn kaiú tarachðé twðn ejkklhsiwðn,
ijdiavzein kaiú metaú twðn 1Ioudaivwn ejpiteleiðn toú
pavsca, touðton hJ aJgiva suvnodoû ejnteuðqen hjdh ajllovtrion
eækrine thðû ejkklhsivaû. wJû ouj movnon eJautwðé aJmartivaû, ajllaú
polloiðû diafqoraðû kaiú diastrofhðû ginovmenon aiætion× kaiú
ouj movnon touúû toiouvtouû kaqaivrei thðû leitourgivaû, ajllaú
kaiú touúû tolmwðntaû touvtoiû koinwneiðn metaú thún kaqaivresin.
 <COL N="0059C"></COL> Touúû deú kaqaireqevntaû ajpostereiðsqai kaiú thðû eæxwqen
timhðû, hßû oJ aåg oû kanwún kaiú toú touð qeouð iJerateiðon meteivlhfen.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0059"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>pa'. Pavntaû touúû eijsiovntaû eijû thún ejkklhsivan touð qeouð,
kaiú twðn iJerwðn grafwðn ajkouvontaû, mhú koinwnouðntaû deú
eujchðû aåma twðé lawðé, hÞ ajpostrefomevnouû thún metavlhyin thðû
eujcaristivaû katav tina ajtaxivan, touvtouû ajpoblhvtouû givnesqai
thðû ejkklhsivaû, eåwû aÞn ejxomologhsavmenoi kaiú deivxanteû
karpouúû metanoivaû, kaiú parakalevsanteû, tuceiðn
dunhqwðsi suggnwvmhû. Mhú ejxeiðnai deú koinwneiðn toiðû ajkoinwthvtoiû
mhdeú kat1 oiækouû sunelqovntaû suneuvcesqai toiðû
mhú thðé ejkklhsivaé suneucomevnoiû, mhdeú ejn eJtevraé ejkklhsivaé
uJpodevcesqai touúû ejn eJtevraé ejkklhsivaé mhú sunagomevnouû. Eij
deú faneivh tiû twðn ejpiskovpwn hÞ presbuteúrwn hÞ diakovnwn,
hæ tiû touð kanovnoû toiðû ajkoinwnhvtoiû koinwnwðn, kaiú touðton
ajkoinwvnhton eiønai, wJû aÞn sugcevonta toún kanovna thðû
 <COL N="0059D"></COL> ejkklhsivaû.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0059"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>pb'. Eiæ tiû presbuvteroû, hÞ diavkonoû, hÞ oålwû twðn touð
iJerateivou tiû katalipwún thún eJautouð paroikivan, eijû eJtevran
ajpevlqoi, eæpeita pantelwðû metastaúû, diatrivbein ejn ajllhé
paroikivaé peiraðtai ejpiú pollwðé crovnwé, mhkevti leitourgeiðn,
eij mavlista kalouðnti twðé ejpiskovpwé twðé ijdivwé kaiú ejpanelqeiðn
eijû thún paroikivan thún eJautouð parainouðnti mhú uJpakouvoi.
Eij deú kaiú ejpimevnoi thðé ajtaxivaé, pantelwðû aujtoún kaqaireiðsqai
thðû leitourgivaû, wJû mhkevti cwvran eæcein ajpokatastavsewû.
Eij deú kataireqevnta diaú tauvthn thún aijtivan devcoito
eåteroû ejpivskopoû, kajékeiðnon ejpitimivaû tugcavnein uJpoú koinhðû
sunovdou, wJû paraluvonta touúû qesmouúû touúû
ejkklhsiastikouúû
[toún qesmoún thðû ejkklhsivaû].</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0059"><COL N="0061A"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>pg'. Eij tiû ejpivskopoû uJpoú sunovdou kaqaireqeiúû, hÞ
presbuvteroû hÞ diavkonoû uJpoú touð ijdivou ejpiskovpou, tolmhvseievn
ti praðxai thðû leitourgivaû, eiæte oJ ejpivskopoû kataú
thún proavgousan sunhvqeian, eiæte oJ presbuvteroû, eiæte oJ
diavkonoû, mhkevti ejxoún eijnai aujtwðé, mhd1 ejn eJtevraé sunodwðé
ejlpivda ajpokatastavsewû, mhvte ajpologivaû cwvran eæcein×
ajllaú kaiú touúû koinwnouðntaû aujtwðé pavntaû ajpobavllesqai
thðû ejkklhsivaû, kaiú mavlista, eij maqovnteû thún ajpovfasin
thún kataú twðn proeirhmevnwn ejxenecqeiðsan, tolmhvseien aujtoiðû koinwneiðn.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0061"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>pd'. Eiæ tiû presbuvteroû hÞ diavkonoû, katafronhvsaû touð
ejpiskovpou touð ijdivou, ajfwvrisen eJautoún thðû ejkklhsivaû,
kaiú ijdivaé sunhvgagen, kaiú qusiasthvrion eæsthsen [eæphxe], kaiú
touð ejpiskovpou proskalesamevnou ajpeiqoivh, kaiú mhú bouvloito
aujtwðé peivqesqai, mhdeú uJpakouvein kaiú prwðton kaiú
 <COL N="0061B"></COL> deuvteron kalouðnti, touðton kaqaireiðsqai pantelwðû, kaiú
mhkevti qerapeivaû tugcavnein [tuceiðn], mhdeú duvnasqai
lambavnein thún eJautouð timhvn× eij deú paramevnoi qorrubwðn
kaiú ajnastatwðn thún ejkklhsivan, diaú thðû eæxwqen ejxousivaû wJû
stasiwvdh aujtoún ejpistrevfesqai.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0061"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>pe'. Eiæ tiû uJpoú touð ijdivou ejpiskovpou ajkoinwvnhtoû gevgonen,
mhú provteron aujtoún par1 eJtevrwn [eJtevrou] decqhðnai,
eij mhú uJp1 aujtouð paradecqeivh touð ijdivou ejpiskovpou, hÞ sunovdou
genomevnhû, ajpanthvsaû ajpologhvsetai, peivsaû te thún
suvnodon, katadevxoito eJtevran ajpovfasin. 2O aujtoúû deú oåroû
ejpiú laiçkwðn kaiú presbutevrwn kaiú diakovnwn kaiú pavntwn twðn
ejn twðé kanovni.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0061"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>p¾'. Mhdevna aneu eijrhnikwðn devcesqai twðn xevnwn.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0061"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>pz'. Mhdeú presbutevrouû touúû ejn taiðû cwvraiû kanonikaúû
 <COL N="0061C"></COL> ejpistolaúû didovnai, hÞ proúû movnouû touúû geivtonaû
ejpiskovpouû ejpistolaúû ejkpevmpein× touúû deú ajnepilhvptouû
cwrepiskovpouû, didovnai eijrhnikavû.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0061"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ph'. Touúû kaq1 eJkavsthn ejparcivan ejpiskovpouû eijdevnai
crhú toún ejn thðé mhtropovlei proestwðta ejpivskopon, kaiú thún
frontivda ajnadevcesqai pavshû thðû ejparcivaû, diaú toú ejn
